      "gap": "Preserve the source variant of the entry: state and prove thm:p15-weighted-martingale-law at the scope of the source's Exercise 4.4.11 (Durrett 2019, p. 239), which continues only the notation of Exercise 4.4.10: for a martingale X_n with increments xi_m = X_m - X_{m-1} (X_0 only integrable; the source does not assume EX_0^2 < infinity), weights b_m increasing to infinity with sum_m E xi_m^2 / b_m^2 < infinity imply X_n/b_n -> 0 a.s., and in particular E xi_n^2 <= K < infinity with sum_m b_m^{-2} < infinity implies X_n/b_n -> 0 a.s. The handbook statement (body lines 233-246) assumes that X is a square-integrable martingale, i.e. adds the hypothesis EX_0^2 < infinity, a narrowed variant that omits martingales with X_0 in L^1 but not in L^2, which the source's statement covers; the annex proof (lines 347-370) uses only that X_0 is finite, so statement and proof must be given at the source's scope.",
